  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Hola a todos, espero que todo vaya bien!!\n\nVed claims to be a pro at programming, but his friend Varun disagrees. To settle the debate, they decided to seek advice from their mentor. The mentor proposed a simple challenge:\n\nVed must write a program containing NNN lines of code. When the code is compiled, the compiler will indicate how many of those lines have errors, denoted as MMM. Based on the results:\n\n\nIf errors are present in at least **half** of the total lines, Ved will be labeled as a NEWBIE\\text{NEWBIE}NEWBIE.\nOtherwise, he will be called a PRO\\text{PRO}PRO\nAfter compiling Ved's code, the compiler reported errors in MMM lines. Determine Ved's skill category based on this evaluation.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe input contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of lines of code written by Ved and the number of lines of code containing errors, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput PRO\\text{PRO}PRO if Ved is pro, else output NEWBIE\\text{NEWBIE}NEWBIE.\n\n\nIt is allowed to print each character in either case. pro,pRo,PRo\\text{pro}, \\text{pRo}, \\text{PRo}pro,pRo,PRo will all be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "1≤M≤10001 \\leq M \\leq 10001≤M≤1000",
      "M≤NM \\leq NM≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10 6",
        "output": "NEWBIE",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere were 101010 lines and Ved has errors in 666 of them. Since 6≥56 \\ge 56≥5, where 555 is half of 101010, Ved is a newbie due to having errors in at least half the lines."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "9 4",
        "output": "PRO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nHalf of 999 is 4.54.54.5. Ved has errors in less than half the lines, thus he is a pro."
      }
    ]
  },
